  "body": "Tucked away in one of the East Coast Bays most coveted coastal pockets and just two minutes from Waiake beach, this is the kind of property that makes you feel at home the moment you arrive.\r\n\r\nBeautifully presented, warm and full of character, with modern features and a personality that is increasingly hard to find. Beautiful timber floors, a fabulous modern kitchen and seamless indoor-outdoor flow on both sides of the home open to sunny decking and a beautifully landscaped, private garden. Complete with a spa, firepit area and lawn, there is loads of space to relax, entertain, play or simply enjoy the peace and tranquility.\r\n\r\nThree generous double bedrooms offer plenty of flexibility, with one featuring its own ensuite — ideal for teenagers, guests or those wanting a little extra privacy. The stylish bathrooms feature floor-to-ceiling tiling and underfloor heating. Practicality hasn't been overlooked either, with plenty of storage and a garage that offers more than just parking. A versatile additional area is currently set up as a gym, rumpus or man cave — perfect for hobbies, teenagers or working out.\r\n\r\nPositioned on the northern side of sought-after Sharon Road, you can stroll in either direction to Waiake or Browns Bay beaches, with cafés, restaurants and shops close by. Excellent public transport provides access to the wider North Shore and CBD, while a choice of excellent public and private schools is within easy reach.\r\n\r\nWhether you're stepping onto or up the property ladder, looking for an easy-care executive home or downsizing without compromising on lifestyle, this is a very special opportunity. Definitely a secret gem that's worth discovering.\r\n\r\nTo be sold by way of Auction (unless sold prior), 1.30pm, Thursday 22nd October, Bayleys Corner 2 - 8 Northcroft Street, Takapuna, Auckland\r\n\r\nAll agents welcome - conjunctions invited. NB. Some images have been digitally enhanced.\r\nMarketed by: Tara Menzies and Cindy Leong",
